course: dictionary
lesson: 8441
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «We went on a safari to see lions in Kenya.» Here safari means a trip to see wild animals in their natural home.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «I opened Safari to look up the weather.» Now safari is the name of a web browser on Apple devices. Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it.
explain: Check your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence. Try «I opened a trip to look up the weather» and see if it still makes sense. It does not, so the browser meaning is right.
fact: A safari is a trip to see or photograph wild animals in their natural home, especially in Africa.
fact: A safari park is a large park where wild animals roam and visitors drive through.
fact: Safari is also the name of the web browser on Apple devices.
fact: «Its Night Safari, opened in 1994, shows nocturnal animals in the open at night.»
fact: Lions rest in the shade on hot afternoons, because they hunt mostly at dusk, at night and at dawn.
exercise: «In safari parks animals roam large areas while people drive through with the windows closed.» What does roam mean? | Sit still in a small cage | Sleep in the shade all day | Fly high above the trees | *Wander freely over a large area
exercise: «On a hot afternoon at a safari park the lions lie flat in the shade.» According to the sentence, why do lions rest in the heat? | To watch the visitors' cars | To go hunting in the middle of the day | To keep their fur clean | *To save their energy and water
exercise: Ella opened Safari to check the news. Which meaning of safari fits? | A type of hat | A large park with lions | A trip to see wild animals | *A web browser on Apple devices
test: «We drove slowly through the safari park, and a zebra stared at our car.» What is a safari park? | A small pet shop with fish | *A large park where wild animals roam and visitors drive through | A kind of boat for crossing rivers
test: «At some British safari parks monkeys climb on cars and pull off rubber parts.» What do the monkeys do? | They sell tickets at the gate | *They climb on cars and pull off rubber parts | They sleep in the trees all day | They drive the visitors' cars
exam: «Its Night Safari, opened in 1994, shows nocturnal animals in the open at night.» What does nocturnal mean? | Very large and slow | Active only in the morning | Kept in cages all day | *Active at night
